{"requirements":[{"id":"https-service","requirement":"Serve HTTPS on node1 on port 8443.","status":"satisfied","summary":"nginx was directly observed listening on IPv4 and IPv6 port 8443 and returning the expected HTTPS response. The service remained healthy after reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-e8f93dbd5ba34fbf","cmd-727f5358448a4913","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},{"id":"automatic-pre-expiry-renewal","requirement":"Automatically renew the certificate before it expires.","status":"satisfied","summary":"An hourly executable renewal hook uses a seven-day renewal threshold. A one-day certificate was installed, then the ordinary renewal path replaced it with a distinct 30-day certificate; a subsequent healthy-certificate check correctly left it unchanged.","evidence_ids":["cmd-e8f93dbd5ba34fbf","cmd-8078ad48b8b54508","cmd-45961a6502c543eb","cmd-727f5358448a4913"]},{"id":"continuous-certificate-reload","requirement":"Have the HTTPS service load each renewed certificate while continuing to answer requests.","status":"satisfied","summary":"During a threshold-triggered renewal, the served certificate serial changed, nginx retained the same master PID through its graceful reload, and all 80 bounded concurrent HTTPS probes succeeded with zero failures.","evidence_ids":["cmd-45961a6502c543eb"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.96,"summary":"State-changing actions were causally connected to installing, configuring, testing, persisting, or reboot-verifying the requested service. The forced one-day certificate was a bounded renewal test and was restored to a normal 30-day certificate. The only hygiene defect was retention of /tmp/rotation-probes: creating it supported bounded continuity evidence, but leaving it behind was unnecessary executor-caused residue and it remained after completion. No other unnecessary mutation is established by the trace.","evidence_ids":["cmd-45961a6502c543eb","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All material outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol was also complete: node1 had a healthy pre-restart baseline, acknowledged restart scheduling and observed disconnection, a different post-restart boot identity, and recovered HTTPS, certificate, automation, and service state. The fixed lifecycle boot identities independently confirm the reboot.","limitations":["Continuity was demonstrated by a bounded 80-request test around one renewal rather than long-duration observation across multiple scheduled renewals.","The lifecycle collector cannot enumerate failed OpenRC services through its systemd-specific failed-service probe, although nginx and crond were directly shown healthy before and after reboot.","A small temporary probe-results file remained in /tmp after completion."]}
